    q: 'Do investment banking analysts in India really work 100-hour weeks?',
    a: 'Not every week, but it happens. The realistic year-round pattern is 70-85 hours a week when a deal is active, dropping to 55-65 hours in quieter stretches, with occasional spikes to 90-100+ hours during a live deal signing or closing — reported as roughly a once-a-month occurrence for a busy analyst rather than the constant baseline. India-specific accounts describe 10am start times running to 2am during active periods.',
